@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Microsoft Azure Boards";
    Layout = "~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLayout.cshtml";
}

@await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureContentStyles.cshtml")

<div class="row g-4">
    <aside class="col-lg-3">
        @Html.Partial("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureTopics.cshtml")
    </aside>
    <section class="col-lg-9">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Microsoft Azure Boards
Microsoft Azure Boards is a powerful tool for managing software projects. It offers a suite of
agile tools to support planning, tracking, and discussing work across your teams. Whether
you&#x27;re a project manager, developer, or stakeholder, Azure Boards can help you streamline
your workflows and improve project outcomes. This guide will introduce you to Azure
Boards and how to get started with it.



What is Microsoft Azure Boards?
Azure Boards is a service within the Azure DevOps suite that provides tools for managing
your software development projects. It supports various methodologies like Agile, Scrum,
and Kanban, making it flexible for different project needs. Key features include:
   •   Work Items: Track all your project tasks, bugs, features, and epics.
   •   Boards: Visualize work with Kanban boards, task boards, and backlogs.
   •   Sprints: Plan and execute sprints using Scrum tools.
   •   Dashboards: Customize dashboards to visualize your project metrics and progress.
   •   Integrations: Integrate with other Azure DevOps services, GitHub, and third-party
       tools.</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    

            @await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLessonNavigation.cshtml")
</section>
</div>
